{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And it came to pass, when the days were long for him there.</b> Days of marital relations; and therefore it was permitted to him to engage in marital relations. And so we find with Hilkiyahu the priest, father of Jeremiah, who lay with his wife by day, because he had not lain with her for many days." "<b>And Avimelekh looked out through the window.</b> One may say: not that the window was open, but rather since it was locked, Avimelekh understood the matter — for in a dark house it is permitted to engage in marital relations even by day. And since the famine was only in that land alone, marital relations were permitted to him." "<b>And he looked, and behold, Yitzhak was laughing.</b> Laughing that precedes intercourse, as it is written: ״The man, the Hebrew, was brought in to us לצחק בנו״ (to play with us), and after it is written: ״לשכב עמי״ (to lie with me). And one should not say that he saw him engaging in intercourse, for Yitzhak would not do such a thing before onlookers and by day."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:06:04.349800156Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}